---
// Cascade probe — VARIANT C (MEASURE-3, D-02 claim 3).
//
// Import shape: the design system's `tokens.css` from this frontmatter,
// `theme-charcoal.css` from a HYDRATED ISLAND (`ThemeCssIsland.tsx`).
//
// Variant C matters on its own, independently of the ordering question:
// Astro hoists island CSS out of the island into a page-level stylesheet, so
// it competes in the SAME cascade bucket as an `.astro` import. There is no
// separate island cascade. A theme delivered by a component rather than by a
// layout is therefore subject to exactly the same tie, and that is not
// obvious from the outside — it is the kind of thing a team assumes is
// isolated until a colour changes.
//
// The `client:load` directive below is load-bearing and must not be removed to
// quieten `check-no-js.sh`. Without it the component is server-rendered and
// the island path is never exercised, which would make this variant a
// duplicate of A rather than a distinct measurement. `check-no-js.sh` excludes
// this route BY NAME for that reason.
//
// THE ORDER OF THE TWO IMPORT LINES BELOW IS LOAD-BEARING, and the reason is
// a measured finding rather than a style preference. With the COMPONENT import
// first, this page emits charcoal before tokens; moving the `tokens.css` line
// above it flips the emitted order to tokens before charcoal (measured both
// ways, INLINE_CSS=never, 2026-08-17). So an island's position in the page
// cascade is decided by where the COMPONENT's import statement sits in the
// page — not by the fact that it is an island, and not by anything about the
// island itself. Being hoisted does not mean being last.
//
// Keep the component import first. It is what makes casc-c emit
// charcoal-then-tokens while casc-d emits tokens-then-charcoal, so the island
// half of the matrix covers BOTH orders instead of testing one order twice.
// Reformatting these two lines — an import sorter, a lint autofix — silently
// halves the matrix while leaving the probe green.
//
// See casc-a.astro for the full note on why the matrix is constructed.

import ThemeCssIsland from "../../components/ThemeCssIsland.tsx";

import "@akhil-saxena/design-system/tokens.css";
---

<html lang="en" data-brand="charcoal">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>probe/casc-c — tokens in .astro, theme from an island</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<h1>casc-c</h1>
		<p>tokens.css from frontmatter; theme-charcoal.css hoisted out of a hydrated island.</p>
		<ThemeCssIsland client:load />
	</body>
</html>
